# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only mvnw, .mvn, pom.xml and src, so nothing else could
# reach the image today. This file is the guard against that changing: the moment
# somebody writes `COPY . .`, the entries below are what stops real secrets and a
# stale host build from being baked into a published image.

# Secrets. application.properties does `spring.config.import=optional:file:.env`,
# so a .env inside the image would silently become the running configuration --
# with this repository's real database, mail, Cloudinary and Paystack credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host build output. Copying it in would let a jar built on somebody's laptop,
# against whatever they had checked out, end up in the image instead of the one
# the build stage produces.
target/

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Editor and IDE state.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.settings/
.classpath
.project

# Documentation and local notes: nothing here affects the build.
docs/
README.md

# Docker's own files.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
